🧮 3️⃣1️⃣ GATE-Style Problem

A car travels:

120 km at 60 km/h

180 km at 90 km/h


Find average speed.

First time:

\[
120/60=2h
\]

Second:

\[
180/90=2h
\]

Total distance:

\[
300km
\]

Total time:

\[
4h
\]

Therefore:

\[
\boxed{75km/h}
\]


---

🧮 3️⃣2️⃣ Another

A person travels half the distance at 30 km/h and half at 60 km/h.

Average:

\[
\frac{2(30)(60)}{30+60}
\]

\[
\boxed{40km/h}
\]

Not:

\[
45km/h
\]

🚨 Equal distance ≠ arithmetic average.


